From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phone libssc: add one-way metadata-only discovery guard

Reuse the original libssc discovery and attribute constructors, without opening
measurement streams. The phone probe locks a process-wide policy before creating
clients. The actual send boundary only admits bounded SUID queries for registry,
accel, ambient_light, gyro and mag, or one-shot attribute reads; both reject
update subscriptions, malformed payloads and unknown fields. All measurement,
disable and other request IDs are refused before packing/sending QMI data.

The lock cannot be disabled through its API. Ordinary original-library behavior
is unchanged until that explicit lock. The dedicated probe is a separate artifact
and uses an internal discovery deadline; a hard process/service bound is still
required around the original synchronous release/close callbacks.

Tests exercise actual protobuf decoding and the real send path with a QMI stub
that aborts if an unreviewed request reaches it. Original delivery encoding tests
remain. This is offline source work, not sensor sample/hardware acceptance.

